A typical univariate linear regression would be of the form

  y ~ normal(alpha * x + beta, sigma);

where x is data and alpha and beta are parameters.  Are
you trying to code a measurement error model in x, as in:

  x_obs ~ normal(x, tau);
  y ~ normal(alpha * x + beta, sigma);

x is true x, x_obs is x observed with measurement error tau,
and y is then modeled using x.  There's a chapter in the manual
that goes over basic measurement error models in the predictors.

