It can lead to biases, but if you only ave a couple occasionally
you should be OK (Michael may say differently).

You should also simulate data from the model and make sure you
can recover the parameters with the expected coverage (e.g., 50% of
parameters fall in the 50% intervals [assuming binomial distribution]).

- Bob

