Whether analytical variability is stable is a domain specific question typically answered by running standard samples on a regular basis, though that is instrument dependent.  For a first pass I would assume yes, I might ask for measurements of standards for a second pass and model it, but always include model checks on that assumption. Depending on the instrument or assay  calibration can be a beast and not everyone understands the role it plays or wants to do it on the suggested schedule. Krzysztof

