Can't the problem also be that adaptation has failed?  I
take it you then think that's a serious enough problem that it
has to be dealt with?

How much diffuse init is enough?  I imagine the problems with
adaptation will vary depending on the scale of the inits in
the unconstrained space (now uniform(-2, 2) by default).  What
if users have their own inits, maybe with some noise?  Should we
just not trust any of the results because other independent chains
initialized elsewhere might diverge?

- Bob

