I'm usually always using CmdStan. It's such a lightweight wrapper that it's easy to change a bit of the math library and see the changes percolate all the way through without needing to do much to rebuild.

If you're wanting to get that set up, follow these directions: https://github.com/stan-dev/cmdstan/wiki/Getting-Started-with-CmdStan
You can do the same with the math library (that was probably written before we split out the math submodule).

I haven't been successful getting gdb running, but that might be cause I'm on a Mac. I think Ben might have gotten it up and running.

Daniel

