Thanks Bob. I am already looking at what you call 'beta_tilde' in my code. This is what differs from the individual study-level estimates. I do this using,

beta_tilde = normal_rng(a,sigma);
  while(beta_tilde<0) beta_tile = normal_rng(a,sigma);

where I need the while loop to ensure that I get a positive value of this parameter.

The trouble is that the bulk of probability mass for a -- the population level parameter -- is sometimes nowhere near bulk of mass for the beta[i]s. This means that I get an estimated beta_tilde that is not close to the individual beta[i]s.

